course: dictionary
lesson: 11483
title: Affixed: stuck on and added
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Affixed is a formal word, so you may meet it in instructions or exam questions. It means fixed, stuck or attached to something. «The label was affixed to the box.» The clue is the word label: a label is stuck on, so affixed means stuck on.
explain: In everyday talk, people say «stuck on» or «attached» instead. If you see «a notice affixed to the school gate», you can swap in «a notice stuck to the school gate» and the sentence still makes sense. That is a good check.
explain: In grammar, an affix is a part added to a word to make a new word. A prefix goes at the front, like un- in «unhappy». A suffix goes at the end, like -ful in «careful». Affixed means added in this way, so grammar books use it when they talk about these word parts.
fact: Affixed means fixed, stuck or attached to something.
fact: «The label was affixed to the box» means the label was stuck on the box.
fact: An affix is a part added to a word, such as a prefix (un-) or a suffix (-ful).
fact: Affix is a verb, and affixed is its past form: affix, affixes, affixing, affixed.
fact: In everyday talk, use «stuck on» or «attached» instead of affixed.
exercise: «The sign was affixed to the gate.» What does affixed mean here? | Read out loud | Taken away for ever | *Stuck on or attached | Painted in bright colours
exercise: In the word «careful», what is -ful? | A type of paper | A whole new sentence | *A suffix added to the end | A prefix added to the front
exercise: «The label was affixed to the box.» Which everyday words could replace affixed? | *Stuck on or attached | Lifted off or removed | Put in the bin | Read aloud
test: «The notice was affixed to the school wall.» Which word means the same as affixed? | Sang | Hidden | Spilled | *Attached
test: In the word «unkind», what is un-? | A full stop | A suffix added to the end | *A prefix added to the front | A word that means kind
exam: Which sentence uses affixed correctly? | The clock affixed a loud song | She affixed her shoes and ran away | The rain affixed the dog to the bus | *The stamp was affixed to the top corner of the envelope
